WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.220
A machine creates your perfect copy...

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:03.640
but destroys the original.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.780
Would you step inside?

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.640
Imagine walking into a machine.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.390
It scans every atom in your body,
records your memories, your personality,

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.250
and every detail of your brain.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.150
Then it creates an identical
version of you somewhere else.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.600
Your copy wakes up.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.460
It remembers your childhood,
your friends, your family,

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.130
and everything you've ever experienced.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.340
To everyone else, that person is you.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.980
But here's the problem:
the original you has been destroyed.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.740
So did you actually travel somewhere?

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.550
Or did you die, while another person
simply inherited your memories?

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.330
If your copy believes it's you,
does that make it you?

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.130
Your family might never
know the difference.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.390
Your copy might continue
your life perfectly.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.580
But would you experience
waking up on the other side?

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:42.820
Would you enter the machine?

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:43.820
Yes or no?

